      "onboarding": {
        "title": "How to add a worker",
        "show": "Show",
        "hide": "Hide",
        "intro": "A worker is a separate process (on this machine or another) that pulls jobs and runs heavy ASR. The Backend does not load Whisper. The worker only dials the Backend over HTTPS — no inbound ports on the worker side.",
        "step1Title": "Decide where it will run.",
        "step1Body": "A local machine for tests, a dedicated VPS or GPU server for production. The worker needs outbound HTTPS to this Backend, ffmpeg, Python 3.12, and about 16 GB RAM (CPU, large-v3) or 8 GB VRAM (GPU).",
        "step2Title": "Install the worker repo.",
        "whisperGpuTitle": "Whisper model and GPU (read this)",
        "whisperGpuBody": "You do not download Whisper by hand. The worker uses faster-whisper: on the first real job (or first model load) it will download the chosen model (e.g. large-v3) from the internet into a local cache — this can take several GB and a few minutes. For GPU: install a current NVIDIA driver and CUDA user-mode stack matching your PyTorch/ctranslate2 build, then `poetry install --with gpu,demucs,dev`, set `WORKER_ASR_DEVICE=cuda` or `auto`, and run `nvidia-smi` to confirm the device. CPU-only: use the `cpu` extra; no GPU software needed. On Linux, also install `ffmpeg` (the worker pipeline expects it for audio).",
        "snippetCpuLabel": "CPU install",
        "snippetCpuBody": "git clone <DotSoundComputeWorker repo URL>\ncd DotSoundComputeWorker\npoetry install --with cpu,dev",
        "snippetGpuLabel": "GPU install (CUDA)",
        "snippetGpuBody": "git clone <DotSoundComputeWorker repo URL>\ncd DotSoundComputeWorker\npoetry install --with gpu,demucs,dev",
        "step3Title": "Create the worker on this page.",
        "step3ListName": "name — any label (e.g. local-dev, vps-eu-1).",
        "step3ListProfile": "profile — gpu_full for the remote_whisper tier in the cascade.",
        "step3ListCidrs": "allowed_ip_cidrs — source IPs the worker dials from. Use presets (Localhost / Private LAN / Allow any).",
        "step3ListConc": "max_concurrent_jobs — how many jobs at once (default 1).",
        "step3After": "On submit, the Backend returns WORKER_SECRET only once. Copy it.",
        "step4Title": "Put credentials in the worker .env",
        "snippetEnvLabel": ".env template",
        "snippetEnvBody": "WORKER_ID=<from step 3>\nWORKER_SECRET=<from step 3>\nWORKER_BACKEND_BASE_URL=https://your.backend.example\nWORKER_DEBUG=false\nWORKER_ASR_MODEL_SIZE=large-v3\nWORKER_ASR_DEVICE=auto\nWORKER_USE_DEMUCS=false\nWORKER_METRICS_PORT=9100",
        "step4After": "The .env file is gitignored; do not commit secrets.",
        "step5Title": "Start the worker",
        "snippetMakeLabel": "foreground (dev)",
        "snippetMakeBody": "make dev",
        "snippetSystemdLabel": "production (systemd)",
        "snippetSystemdBody": "[Service]\nWorkingDirectory=/opt/DotSoundComputeWorker\nEnvironmentFile=/opt/DotSoundComputeWorker/.env\nExecStart=/opt/DotSoundComputeWorker/.venv/bin/python -m worker\nRestart=always\nReadOnlyPaths=/\nRuntimeDirectory=worker-tmp\n[Install]\nWantedBy=multi-user.target",
        "snippetDockerLabel": "docker (CPU)",
        "snippetDockerBody": "docker run -d --name dotsound-worker \\\n  --read-only --tmpfs /tmp:size=2G \\\n  --env-file .env \\\n  -p 9100:9100 \\\n  dotsound-compute-worker:cpu",
        "step6Title": "Verify",
        "step6Body": "Within ~15s the worker row below should look active and last_seen should update. If not, open the worker drawer: auth_fail means wrong secret, 404 means IP not in allowlist.",
        "protocolRef": "Full HMAC and protocol: docs/compute-worker-protocol.md in the Backend repo."
      },
